(D1 - Discrepancy 1 repro: LANGUAGE.md:4884 lists `isn't` and `aren't` as
 accepted spellings of `not`. On 0.4.9 and earlier neither lexed.
 src/lexer/scan.rs:360 mapped "isn't" | "aren't" | "doesn't" | "don't" to
 Token::Not, so the intent was in the compiler - but the scanner split
 the apostrophe off first (it is the possessive marker and the
 quoted-name delimiter, scan.rs:118 and :587), so the contraction never
 reached that keyword table. `doesn't` and `don't` failed identically and
 were not documented.
 RESOLVED, 2026-08-22 - vox #84 ("Each now lexes as the two words it
 stands for - is not and are not - while the four undocumented
 contractions ... were removed rather than woken"). Re-run verbatim
 against 0.4.10: `isn't` now compiles and fires. `doesn't`/`don't` remain
 refused, correctly (never documented).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D1.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   isnt fired
)
